    "question": {
      ":question/id": "56eead1a-b1b9-57db-95cb-563545bb8a55",
      ":question/problem": "A data center initially contains $42$ computers. The number of computers in the data center $C(t)$ increases at a rate that obeys an inhibited growth model, where $t\\ge 0$ is the time in months. If the maximum capacity of the data center is $482$ computers, which differential equation could be used to model the number of computers? Assume that $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "38f515a7-3cf7-506f-84d2-7bf1e00ccd48",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "99082f31-7fa2-5970-a0fd-a0995c393235",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=k(345-C)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "eb3d2e3f-56b1-5081-b09d-d01b6008e932",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=k(441-C)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "c6174afe-4adf-5660-b283-c597833209ff",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=k(405-C)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "55d20102-4cdf-5d6c-a45b-8a2ff9b9ba57",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=k(482-C)"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "6a0d8e76-0a9a-5103-8101-31e8507a38e0",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=k(224-C)"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "55d20102-4cdf-5d6c-a45b-8a2ff9b9ba57"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Since the number of computers in the data center obeys an inhibited growth model, the rate at which the number of computers changes is proportional to the difference between the maximum capacity and the number of computers in the data center. Therefore, we have the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=k(a-C),\n$$\n\nwhere $a$ is the maximum capacity of the data center, and $k>0$ is a constant of proportionality.\n\nIn our case, $a=482$ computers, and we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}C}{\\text{d}t}=k(482-C).\n$$"
    },
